    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "This metric ensures that metadata is accessible using standardized communication protocols that support interoperability and automated retrieval.\n\n**What is being measured?**\n\nWhether the metadata from the Research Object can be retrieved using a standardized, open, and well-documented communication protocol, such as HTTP, HTTPS, OAI-PMH, SPARQL, or REST APIs.\n\n**Why should we measure it?**\n\nWhen metadata is exposed through widely adopted protocols, it ensures that systems and tools—regardless of platform—can automatically access and exchange metadata. \n\n**What must be provided for the measurement?**\n\nThe endpoint where the metadata can be accessed.\n\n**What are considered valid results?**\n\nThe metadata is accessible using a standardized communication protocol (e.g., HTTP, HTTPS, OAI-PMH, SPARQL, FTP, REST)."
      }
    ],
